---
description: Use the @/ path alias for imports inside src/ instead of relative paths
alwaysApply: true
---

# Alias imports

In TypeScript/TSX under `src/`, import project modules through the `@/` alias (maps to `src/`). Never use relative imports (`./` or `../`).

```ts
// ❌ BAD
import { concatPcm } from "../audio/pcm";
import { useDictation } from "./useDictation";

// ✅ GOOD
import { concatPcm } from "@/voice/audio/pcm";
import { useDictation } from "@/app/useDictation";
```

- Applies to type-only imports too: `import type { VoiceState } from "@/voice/session/state";`
- Package imports (`react`, `@tauri-apps/api/...`, `@supabase/supabase-js`) are unchanged.
- When editing a file that still has relative imports, convert them in the same change.
- Exception: `supabase/functions/**` runs on Deno and is deployed per-function without the Vite alias; keep its imports self-contained.
- The alias is defined in `tsconfig.json` (`paths`) and `vite.config.ts` (`resolve.alias`); keep both in sync if it changes.
